                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1198be10-8704-3db1-919f-0471f6fa4439",
                        "entry_id": "c0305ceb-a2c7-3469-9fb1-796414a91c00",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действие по значению гл. передразнивать, передразнить; воспроизведение (обычно в комическом виде) чьих-либо движений, слов, манеры поведения и т. п."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d30675c3-cc8c-446e-b4d2-c533420dc0e3",
                                "sense_id": "1198be10-8704-3db1-919f-0471f6fa4439",
                                "text": "Я никак не могу понять, что вы находите в этом забавного и какое вам может доставлять удовольствие передразнивание моего кашля."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "972072bb-aaca-4d3f-a304-2f1a44b4787d",
                                "sense_id": "1198be10-8704-3db1-919f-0471f6fa4439",
                                "text": "И тогда дурашливость обретет новые краски: ярко выраженная подростковая агрессия ― это ведь тоже передразнивание взрослых с их матом, татуировками, экспрессивной мимикой и жестами."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "01364ed6-0385-4c82-a59d-41d99c6d3495",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0305ceb-a2c7-3469-9fb1-796414a91c00",
                        "source_sense_id": "1198be10-8704-3db1-919f-0471f6fa4439",
                        "target_lang_word": "mimicry",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mimicry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33386152-654d-3024-87af-40662c75dee0",
                                        "entry_id": "bd95a54e-0cab-3a14-83b1-7710239c3674",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act or ability to simulate or effect the appearance, characteristics, or behavior of someone or something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1703101-acba-4f29-b8ff-24c6726310d1",
                                                "sense_id": "33386152-654d-3024-87af-40662c75dee0",
                                                "text": "They say that mimicry is the sincerest form of flattery, but I still think I'm being mocked when he acts just like me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84711707-1225-41a2-b8d0-5cbba94cdd9b",
                                                "sense_id": "33386152-654d-3024-87af-40662c75dee0",
                                                "text": "When animal mimicry goes really wrong they don't just look like something that a predator would ignore, they look like lunch."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c8394b37-1cc7-428e-abec-80384efb1c54",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0305ceb-a2c7-3469-9fb1-796414a91c00",
                        "source_sense_id": "1198be10-8704-3db1-919f-0471f6fa4439",
                        "target_lang_word": "mimicking",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mimicking",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6a98ce8-f794-3763-8514-bf2fe5f388d1",
                                        "entry_id": "75dc79a1-3307-34ae-8270-bf7f75916668",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "gerund of mimic: mimicry; (countable) an instance of this."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "279c0e21-8f39-487a-a417-34fee840494a",
                                                "sense_id": "d6a98ce8-f794-3763-8514-bf2fe5f388d1",
                                                "text": "They had a thousand odd stories and jokes about the events of the day, and burlesque descriptions and mimickings of the spectators who had been admiring them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77863416-836e-436c-8e95-cd8a27ab8e8c",
                                                "sense_id": "d6a98ce8-f794-3763-8514-bf2fe5f388d1",
                                                "text": "Many within our community view childrearing with skepticism or disdain. Affirmatively choosing parenting as a gay man or lesbian is often seen as a retreat from public activism to private life or as a mimicking of heterosexuality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mimicking",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2384778-94a5-399e-b8ea-ff8d11bc9d84",
                                        "entry_id": "d1c5de39-009a-3aa5-ba82-0c05cf1b94dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of mimic"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2d666474-39a4-441d-8150-c695e5b9f22b",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0305ceb-a2c7-3469-9fb1-796414a91c00",
                        "source_sense_id": "1198be10-8704-3db1-919f-0471f6fa4439",
